# Shortcut: КМП

When the user says **КМП** (or «кмп»):
1. Create a git commit (short Russian one-liner, repo style)
2. Immediately `git push` to the tracked remote — do **not** ask whether to push
3. If there is nothing to commit but unpushed commits exist — just push
4. After push, briefly confirm commit hash + that it was pushed

# Commit messages

When generating a git commit message (including Source Control "Generate Commit Message"):

## Format
- One short line only, usually 3–8 words (max ~50–60 characters)
- Russian, matching this repo
- No bullet lists, no Summary/Test plan, no conventional-commit prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`)
- No trailing period
- No second paragraph / commit body

## Be concrete
- Name the specific UI/feature that changed (свайп назад, словарь финансов, popover создать, статус проекта…)
- Prefer the concrete what/why over vague polish words
- Look at the actual diff; do not invent a generic summary

Avoid abstract phrasing like:
- Улучшить стили и анимацию
- Обновить стили и улучшить функционал
- Фиксы UI
- Мелкие правки
- Improve UX / update styles

Prefer specific phrasing like:
- Затемнить подложку свайпа назад
- Словарь подсказок в настройках
- Кламп popover к колонке на ПК
- Статус и цвет в конец проекта
- Заблокировать landscape в TMA

If several unrelated changes are staged, name the main user-facing one (still one short line).
